{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-portability","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds Bash wrappers and prompt-side snippets that must remain Bash 3.2-safe under set -euo pipefail.","prompt_body":"Investigate shell portability and failure-control behavior in the new wrapper, SKILL.md bash snippets, and harnesses. Pay close attention to array expansion, mktemp usage, printf -v, command substitution under set -e, unset variables under set -u, and values containing whitespace. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bootstrap-contract","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The extraction creates a new contract boundary between implement-bootstrap.sh, implement-bootstrap-invoke.sh, and the /implement orchestrator.","prompt_body":"Verify that initial and resume modes preserve the existing bootstrap semantics, argv assembly, exit propagation, and IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR pass-through. Check that callers do not reformat exit-2 messages, that non-2 failures remain visible correctly, and that dirty-tree recovery re-enters through the intended resume path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"routing-envelope","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The wrapper filters and dual-writes routing keys that drive later /implement decisions before session-env rehydration.","prompt_body":"Audit the routing envelope key set, stdout emission, bootstrap-routing.env write, and SKILL.md parsing logic for dropped keys, stale values, precedence mistakes, and fallback failures. Check consumers before session-env rehydration, especially degraded-tools gate, dirty-tree resume, branch state, repo selection, and coder routing. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"redaction-boundary","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The new wrapper centralizes stderr redaction and writes files under session tmpdirs, creating security-sensitive boundaries.","prompt_body":"Review secret and tmpdir redaction paths, stderr/stdout separation, temporary-file handling, and writes to bootstrap-routing.env for leaks or unsafe trust assumptions. Consider missing tmpdirs, symlinks, attacker-controlled bootstrap stdout, and failures inside the redaction pipeline. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"prompt-orchestration","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The change rewrites load-bearing orchestration prose and embedded bash that future agents will follow literally.","prompt_body":"Inspect the SKILL.md and shared documentation changes as executable operator guidance, not just prose. Look for contradictory instructions, stale direct-bootstrap references, missing exports, duplicated parse blocks drifting apart, or anti-halt and dirty-tree wording that could make an agent bypass the wrapper. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-wiring","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The change relies on new and retargeted offline harnesses plus Makefile shard wiring to prevent regressions.","prompt_body":"Check that the new harness actually exercises the promised contract and that Makefile, .md siblings, and structural pins cover the new wrapper without masking failures. Look for brittle greps, false positives, missing executable assumptions, incorrect shard wiring, and tests that pass with an incomplete or wrong implementation. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
